  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe makes about 16 cups of soup or 8 (2-cup) servings.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce",
      "secondary_message": "4 stick celery\n1 small bunch Italian (flat-leaf) parsley\n1 bunch kale"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, trim, and medium dice carrots. Place in a large bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim and slice celery crosswise into ¼-inch thick pieces. Add to the bowl with the carrots.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, halve, and small dice onions; peel and mince garlic. Add both to the bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "5 clove garlic"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large pot over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the pot is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add veggies and spices; cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 10 minutes. (Reserve bowl for later use.) \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp extra virgin olive oil\n1 tbsp Italian seasoning\n1 ½ tsp basil, dried\n1 ¼ tsp salt\n1 tsp rosemary, dried\n¾ tsp black pepper\n½ tsp crushed red pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, rinse and drain lentils.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 ½ cups green lentils, dried"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the veggies are softened, add lentils, broth, tomatoes, and bay leaves to the pot; stir to combine the soup, cover, and bring to a boil over high heat (skim away any foam that rises to the surface). Once boiling, uncover, reduce to a simmer, and cook, stirring occasionally and breaking up the tomatoes with a spoon, until lentils are tender and soup has thickened slightly, 25-30 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "10 cups vegetable broth\n1 (794 g) can canned whole tomatoes"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, shave parsley leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Place in the reserved bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Fold kale leaves in half lengthwise and slice off the stems; chop or tear leaves into bite-sized pieces. Add to the bowl with the parsley.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the lentils are done, add parsley and kale to the pot in handfuls, waiting for the greens to wilt slightly before adding the next handful. Continue to cook until kale is completely wilted, 2-3 minutes more.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add vinegar to the pot, stir to combine, and remove from heat.",
      "secondary_message": "1 ½ tbsp red wine vinegar"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide soup between bowls and enjoy!\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
